--- a/server/README.md
+++ b/server/README.md
@@ -157,3 +157,18 @@ The agreed AI contract remains a later backend integration around `POST /trips/:
 Phase 5 adds backend-owned group membership for `GROUP` trips: group creation, leader/member authorization, expiring invitation tokens, join/leave/remove-member flows, and automatic group closure when a trip ends. The backend deliberately does not generate QR images; clients or the separately owned QR component can encode the returned `inviteToken`.
 
 Routes are under `/api/v1/groups`. Invitation tokens are returned only when created; only SHA-256 token hashes are persisted.
+
+
+## Phase 6 - Tracking, Maps boundary and realtime
+
+Phase 6 accepts GPS updates only for active trips and only from authorized, consenting participants. Trusted points are persisted, the latest trusted location is maintained separately, group location reads require active membership, and `location:updated` is emitted through authenticated Socket.IO trip/group rooms.
+
+Routes:
+
+- `POST /api/v1/tracking/pings` — validate and store a trusted GPS point.
+- `GET /api/v1/tracking/me/latest?tripId=...` — return the caller's latest trusted point.
+- `POST /api/v1/tracking/trips/:tripId/consent` — group participant tracking consent.
+- `DELETE /api/v1/tracking/trips/:tripId/consent` — revoke group participant tracking consent.
+- `GET /api/v1/groups/:groupId/locations` — authorized group-member location feed.
+
+Socket clients may connect anonymously for the Phase 0 `system:ready` event, but only a valid tourist access token can authorize `tracking:subscribe` and join `trip:{id}` / `group:{id}` rooms. This phase does not call the separate AI/ML or blockchain services. The location records created here are the backend source signals those integrations may consume later.
